/bin/
/tmp/
*.test
.env
.DS_Store
.NOTES.md
# Raw notes from the owner: a scratchpad, in Portuguese, and not a record the
# project keeps. Read against the tree it becomes a spec in docs/plan/.
NOTES.md

# Identidade visual de uma instalacao especifica. O modelo versionado e
# `brand.example.yaml`; o arquivo real e do cliente, nao do repositorio.
/brand.yaml

# go.work lets you point cmd/brevis-sdk at the local sdk while developing.
# It stays out of the repo: cmd/brevis-sdk/go.mod must require the published
# SDK, because `go install pkg@version` refuses a module carrying replace
# directives -- which is exactly how the CLI is meant to be installed.
go.work
go.work.sum

# Binários compilados dos comandos. `go build -o brevis` dentro de cmd/brevis-sdk
# deixa um de 30 MB ali, e um deles entrou no repositório na v0.4.1 e seguiu
# sendo recommitado. Artefato de build não é fonte.
/cmd/brevis-sdk/brevis-sdk
/brevis

# Python build and test artefacts. `python -m build` leaves a wheel and an
# sdist in lib/python-context/dist/, `uv run` leaves a .venv and a lock, and
# pytest leaves its caches. None of it is source, and the lock in particular
# would pin a dev tool's resolution into a library that declares no
# dependencies at all.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
/lib/python-context/dist/
/lib/python-context/.venv/
/lib/python-context/uv.lock
